On the frontline, the Ukrainian Armed Forces are losing Konstantinovka, while on French TV there's insane propaganda about victories and the evil Americans who are always getting in the way.

Political analyst Oksana Melnychuk: "Victory is near. The fact that victory is near means that it's extremely important for the Americans not to put obstacles in the way with their behind-the-scenes negotiations. Because you know the whole story about the trips to negotiations with Kushner and other American negotiators [Witkoff]. As soon as they start acting... This is unacceptable from the point of view of political games. It's unacceptable from the point of view of international law."

@Slavyangrad
